# Correctness over expediency

**Always. No exceptions.**

When schema or API shape conflicts with a quick fix, implement the correct model fully.

## GeekAPI `post_translations` presentation columns

| Column | API field | Use |
|--------|-----------|-----|
| `home_use_case_excerpt` | `homeUseCaseExcerpt` | Home + dept use-case lists |
| `hero_excerpt` | `heroExcerpt` | Pillar, tool, blog hero under title |
| `newspaper_excerpt` | `newspaperExcerpt` | Pillar, tool, blog newspaper wire |
| `pillar_page_use_case_excerpt` | `pillarPageUseCaseExcerpt` | Pillar page content |
| `advertisement` | `advertisement` | NewsArticle / sponsored ad (not an excerpt) |

**One column, one surface.** Publish API accepts and returns all fields; callers populate only what applies per post row.

## Vetoed

- Type-named columns (`blog_excerpt`, `technical_article_excerpt`, `tool_excerpt`, `advertising_excerpt`)
- Merging multiple surfaces into one stored field
- “Map slug prefix → pick one excerpt column” in publish helpers

